PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Round 0 split: 6 colleagues (1-6) pick A (LP fails both entity tests; no LP net-asset figure given; GP holding co. capitalized only by gifts, so unclear whether GP itself or all owners qualify as AIs). 3 colleagues (7-10) pick D (James fails every individual test: $285k combined income < $300k threshold, no asset data; 1% ownership blocks “all owners are AIs” route and no corporate financials shown to meet standalone $5M test). 

Key rule (NI 45-106 s.1.1): entity qualifies if (i) net assets ≥$5M on most recent FS or (ii) every interest owner (direct/indirect) is itself an AI. 

Analysis favors D: GP in A received $6M cash → GP itself meets $5M net-asset test and is therefore an AI; thus all four LP owners are AIs and LP qualifies under (ii). D supplies neither corporate FS nor any route for James, so corporation fails both prongs. Unresolved: whether “gifts” affect beneficial ownership chain in A; whether any implicit net-asset figure can be inferred for D. Current lean: D is the non-AI.}

