PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Round 2 split: 7 favor A (1,2,3,4,5,6,8), 3 favor D (7,9,10). Core disagreement unchanged but sharpened: NI 45-106 s.1.1 entity test is OR (own most-recent FS net assets ≥$5M OR every direct/indirect interest owner is AI). B meets joint-income (>300k combined both years + continuation); C meets joint net-assets (=5M); E meets entity net-assets (5.2M). 

A supporters: no LP-level FS supplied; GP holding company capitalized only by $6M gifts with unmapped ownership chain, so fails both prongs. D supporters: James's 285k combined income fails every individual test + 1% share blocks all-owners; $10M "gift/transfer" supplies no corporate FS figure, creating identical uncertainty as A's GP. 

New evidence/arguments: $10M lands directly on D's corporate balance sheet (concrete net-asset event qualifying standalone prong irrespective of James); $6M in A funds only GP, leaving LP itself without confirmation. Gift language still raises unresolved ownership-attribution issues for chain mapping in both A and D. Majority view now concedes D's $10M would qualify absent split, but A remains the clearer non-qualifier due to unmapped GP. Lean: A (stronger blocker is LP-level confirmation failure); preserve B/C/E clean tests and prior lean toward D if gifts treated symmetrically.}

